## delete: supercell-000 supercell-002 supercell-003
## labels: quick regression nodata

## Rutile: CREATE_DISPLACEMENTS for finite differences (three
## displacements). The supercell is given as three integers (Quantum
## ESPRESSO inputs, with the k-point mesh from RKLENGTH), chosen by NICE
## with MINDISP (FHI-aims inputs, DISTANCE in bohr), read from a
## structure file (the undisplaced supercell just written: the same
## dataset as the NICE one but for the template), and given as nine
## integers with the default template of the calculator (VASP). The
## datasets and one displaced structure of each code are checked.
crystal library rutile
vibrations
  calculator qe
  create_displacements 2 2 2 rklength 20 template 014_create_displacements_qe-*.scf.in dataset 014_create_displacements_qe.txt
  calculator aims
  create_displacements nice 4 mindisp distance 0.01 template 014_create_displacements_aims-*.in dataset 014_create_displacements_aims.txt
  create_displacements supercell 014_create_displacements_aims-000.in distance 0.01 template 014_create_displacements_sc-*.in dataset 014_create_displacements_sc.txt
  calculator vasp
  create_displacements 1 -1 0 -1 -1 0 0 0 -2 dataset 014_create_displacements_vasp.txt
end
